{"comment_text": {"ja11:0.1": "", "ja11:0.2": "", "ja11:0.3": "", "ja11:0.4": "", "ja11:1.1": "Lucky Spot, the wise and prudent deer-king, kept his herd safe in their journey, while the foolish and careless Black Mark lost his whole herd. ", "ja11:1.2": "", "ja11:1.3": "Here, <i lang='pi' translate='no'>lakkhaṇa</i> has the sense “possessing beautiful or auspicious marks”, and hence “lucky”. The description fits the common Chital or “spotted” deer, who are elegant in form, gregarious, and roam in herds. ", "ja11:1.4": "", "ja11:1.5": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Kāḷa</i> (“dark”) has the opposite sense, “unlucky”. ", "ja11:1.6": "", "ja11:2.1": ""}, "html_text": {"ja11:0.1": "<article id='ja11'><header><ul><li class='division'>{}</li>", "ja11:0.2": "<li>{}</li>", "ja11:0.3": "<li>{}</li></ul>", "ja11:0.4": "<h1 class='sutta-title'>{}</h1></header>", "ja11:1.1": "<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja11:1.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja11:1.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja11:1.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja11:1.5": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja11:1.6": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p></blockquote>", "ja11:2.1": "<p class='endsutta'>{}</p></article>"}, "root_text": {"ja11:0.1": "Jātaka ", "ja11:0.2": "Ekakanipāta ", "ja11:0.3": "Sīlavagga ", "ja11:0.4": "1. Lakkhaṇamigajātaka ", "ja11:1.1": "“Hoti sīlavataṁ attho, ", "ja11:1.2": "paṭisanthāravuttinaṁ; ", "ja11:1.3": "Lakkhaṇaṁ passa āyantaṁ, ", "ja11:1.4": "ñātisaṅghapurakkhataṁ; ", "ja11:1.5": "Atha passasimaṁ kāḷaṁ, ", "ja11:1.6": "suvihīnaṁva ñātibhī”ti. ", "ja11:2.1": "Lakkhaṇamigajātakaṁ paṭhamaṁ. "}, "translation_text": {"ja11:0.1": "Stories of Past Lives 11 ", "ja11:0.2": "The Book of the Ones ", "ja11:0.3": "Ethics ", "ja11:0.4": "The Deer Named Lucky Spot: a past life story ", "ja11:1.1": "The virtuous ones prosper, ", "ja11:1.2": "who live extending protection. ", "ja11:1.3": "See Lucky Spot coming, ", "ja11:1.4": "surrounded by their family circle; ", "ja11:1.5": "then see this Black Mark, ", "ja11:1.6": "bereft of family. ", "ja11:2.1": ""}, "variant_text": {"ja11:0.1": "", "ja11:0.2": "", "ja11:0.3": "", "ja11:0.4": "", "ja11:1.1": "", "ja11:1.2": "paṭisanthāravuttinaṁ → paṭisandhāra … (mr) ", "ja11:1.3": "", "ja11:1.4": "ñātisaṅghapurakkhataṁ → purakkhitaṁ (sya1ed, sya2ed); purekkhitaṁ (mr) ", "ja11:1.5": "", "ja11:1.6": "", "ja11:2.1": "Lakkhaṇamigajātakaṁ → lakkhaṇajātakaṁ (sya1ed, sya2ed, pts-vp-pli1) "}, "reference_text": {"ja11:0.1": "", "ja11:0.2": "", "ja11:0.3": "", "ja11:0.4": "", "ja11:1.1": "bj30.6, dr27.5, ms22J_24, msdiv11, pts-vp-pli1.144", "ja11:1.2": "", "ja11:1.3": "", "ja11:1.4": "", "ja11:1.5": "", "ja11:1.6": "", "ja11:2.1": "ms22J_25"}, "keys_order": ["ja11:0.1", "ja11:0.2", "ja11:0.3", "ja11:0.4", "ja11:1.1", "ja11:1.2", "ja11:1.3", "ja11:1.4", "ja11:1.5", "ja11:1.6", "ja11:2.1"]}